Like, any time you get hit, there's, like, a ton of, uh, of knockback.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:43.260
And I, maybe that makes it feel a little bit more like that.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:50.480
But I, I, for me, um, it, it, it felt not entirely thought out.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:55.780
Yeah, the, the feel of playing as Godzilla, especially at first, I hated it.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:56.860
I thought it was terrible.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.520
I, I don't want to say that it won me over.

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:03.140
But I came around, uh, over time.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:11.680
I did start to feel like they, they did a decent job of, of something you don't see that often, but of making you feel like you're the boss.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.740
And everyone else is, like, the player.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:19.240
Where it's, like, it is hard to take you down for the enemy, at least in the, in the early levels.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.120
And eventually, it, it, things get more dangerous and stuff.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.780
It is hard to take you down.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.900
And it's also really hard for you to avoid hits.

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:28.920
It's, like, things are just shooting at you.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:34.280
You're getting hit. And you've got to, a little bit, like, manage your, manage your health intake.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.020
And make sure, like, ah, I'm picking up health a lot.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.280
Which, sometimes, it's very generous with the health drops.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:43.560
But, like, I, I did feel like you're, you're the boss in the sense that you're really powerful.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:48.620
But also in the sense that, like, you're not as agile as, like, the player normally is.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.600
You're, you're kind of clunky in that sense.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.640
Which is, like, what bothered me at first.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:56.560
One, because it felt like it was impossible for me to die in the first stage.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:02.020
That went away. It definitely felt possible to die when I died a lot later, in later stages.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:09.680
But, um, but two, just because, yeah, you are just this big, giant, the biggest target on the screen.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:13.340
Everything's attacking you, but you're also, like, the most dangerous thing on the screen.

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:19.340
I would just argue that with Godzilla being hit by everything, that sounds great to me.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.300
Like, yeah, he's massive.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:25.560
You see all the times in the movies that, uh, the military throws everything they have at him.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.520
It's not that I think, you know, oh, he shouldn't be taking damage or anything.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.920
It's the knockback thing.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:37.620
Like, I've never seen Godzilla take a missile and be like, I gotta move two steps back to fight off that missile blow.

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:46.920
It's like, in this game, especially because it does the side-scrolling thing where it locks you off from the area you just walked from.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:52.020
You're just always, when you get knocked back, you're kind of, like, put in a corner.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.320
And that's true of whether you're Godzilla or Mothra.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.040
You just kind of get stuck back at the...

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.420
Mothra's even worse.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.380
Yeah, exactly.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:04.700
You get stuck at the closed portion of the side-scrolling map.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:11.400
You don't, like, get pushed forward or anything, which I argue could even be worse, honestly, because then it's like, there's no consequence.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.400
But you just...

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:17.740
I would have taken more health damage than this knockback feature.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:20.320
I would have allowed that instead.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:34.120
Yeah, that was, like, especially in some of the bosses where there's no way to really halt the other kaiju from moving towards you.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:39.280
Like, you can't, like, you can't get spacing down because it's just sort of pushing into you.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:46.700
So that just means that you're going to get locked into a corner for however long the AI decides to push into you before it retreats a little bit.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.280
But, like, it became...

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.620
That was just very frustrating.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.640
Yeah, I think particularly the one boss, which is, like, the easiest one.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:56.920
It's, like, that squid-looking thing.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.420
It's, like, the easiest one, but it...

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.660
For some reason, like, it will always push you in a corner.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.980
Like, the other ones I felt like I could keep at bay a little bit.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.520
But that one was just, like...

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:07.840
It would keep me in a corner.

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:08.840
It wasn't even doing damage.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:13.240
It was hitting me, not doing damage, but, like, would keep me on the left side of the screen.

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:22.580
Very frustrating. All right, so that's Godzilla.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.980
Now let's talk about Mothra for a second.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.780
Mothra was who I moved first.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:35.560
So when I was going through the side-scrolling levels, I actually thought, like, oh, maybe there'll be different kinds of levels, whether you're playing as Mothra or Godzilla.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.340
And Mothra had more of a giant Gradius feel.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.060
You know, like, oh, it's just a giant ship in a Gradius level.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:50.840
And maybe the Godzilla ones will be more, like, destruction-based and having to destroy everything in front of you.

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.840
And there's just an onslaught.

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.380
Whereas Mothra might be more of a shmup.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.060
Mothra is not more of a shmup.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.720
That was me just reading into the situation way too early.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:00.560
Instead, it's the same kinds of levels and stuff.

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:11.060
Except for now you have the ability to fly and hover over or under a ton of stuff to just avoid it if you're lucky enough to not get stuck in a knockback loop.

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.060
What did you guys think of Mothra?

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.360
It definitely felt more shmup.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:26.020
And the one thing that stuck out to me was that, like, one of its primary attacks, you had to use the start button, which I thought was weird.

00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:30.660
Especially that it didn't really, like, carry over between the two of them.

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:34.320
But that was my first impression of Mothra.

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:36.900
It's like, okay, shmup and weird controls.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.740
Well, Godzilla's main attack is also the start button too, right?

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:41.120
Yes, the atomic.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:42.160
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:45.940
But, um, yeah, I thought that Mothra...

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.960
Well, one, we already talked about the knockback, but this is not knockback.

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:50.560
This is, like, reset.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:56.960
It's like you get hit no matter where you are in the screen, it'll reset you exactly to the very bottom left corner no matter what.

00:22:57.900 --> 00:22:59.040
Kind of a weird decision.

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.160
The other thing...

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:01.500
I didn't hate playing as Mothra.

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:06.140
One, because you could fly under or over things a lot.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:07.660
So I kind of skipped some parts and levels.

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:09.680
But there were aspects of it that I hated.

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:10.680
One being the knockback.

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:18.860
Two being the fact that her wings are so high up above her hitbox or whatever, and they don't...

00:23:19.860 --> 00:23:22.640
Like, they stop at the top of the screen.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.600
So really, you...

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:32.980
That, like, when her wings are at the top of the screen, you, like, the body of your main area, your hitbox, is pretty much at the middle of the screen.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:37.760
Which means that anything from the set, from the middle of the screen up, you can't reach.

00:23:38.940 --> 00:23:42.740
Because there's an invisible ceiling right at the top of the screen, apparently, that stops you going.

00:23:42.880 --> 00:23:48.220
Like, really, if you're thinking realistically, you should be able to fly all the way to the top and the wings could just get cut off at the top of the screen.

00:23:48.640 --> 00:23:51.720
Like, and just go, you know, clip into nothing up there or whatever.

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:53.040
But it doesn't let you do that.

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:58.100
So it's very... It's like you only have half the screen to work with, but the enemies have the whole screen to work with.

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:12.380
Yeah, and the only thing that I can think of in terms of, like, why the decision was made to make Mothra get knocked to the floor every time he got hit is to sort of counter the fact that you are more agile.

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:18.760
And I guess just increasing the punishment for getting hit when you have a much smaller hitbox than with Godzilla.

00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:26.700
But I think that could have been handled in a way that didn't feel as, like, as punishing.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:28.520
Like, I get that, yeah, it should be...

00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:34.200
There should be some consequence and some balance and trade-off between the characters.

00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:35.700
But that...

00:24:36.320 --> 00:24:40.760
Like, when you take away my own progress by that much, it just...

00:24:40.760 --> 00:24:55.600
And I did get, like, stun-locked pretty often, like, even in the regular levels, where my life was just draining because I just kept getting hit in the same spot every time without being able to move forward.

00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:57.200
It just, like, that was too much.

00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:10.820
Let's get into those side-scrolling levels now that we've talked about how both characters control, because there's a couple of interesting features here.

00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:19.820
One is that the hexagon tiles are represented by a type of terrain, so you do have different landscapes that you will come across based on where you land.

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:21.600
So, if you cross...

00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:28.760
If you go across these tiles, you'll have to complete their side-scrolling levels and, you know, as one complete stage.

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:37.560
So, one thing that's really cool about that is that if you choose to move the maximum amount of spaces you can, you can move a little further with Mothra than you can with Godzilla,

00:25:37.560 --> 00:25:46.260
it makes it into one extended side-scrolling level, granted that ends at a particular stage and then just fades you into the next one,

00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:50.480
but they must all be completed successfully in order.

00:25:50.560 --> 00:25:52.940
There's no break between them or anything like that.

00:25:53.000 --> 00:26:02.120
So, if you cross from wilderness to volcano to jungle, the first stage will be the wilderness stage, followed by the volcano stage, followed by the jungle stage.

00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:06.920
If you cross wilderness, volcano, volcano, you've just got the same volcano stage twice now.

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:13.680
So, you kind of have to maybe think about which types of terrains you're better off dealing with and which ones you want to cross through,

00:26:13.720 --> 00:26:18.120
so this way you don't have to deal with, if you're me, the volcano levels at all,

00:26:18.140 --> 00:26:28.700
because the volcano itself is very frustrating and something that shoots a significant amount of projectiles that will bury you into the corner of the screen very quickly.

00:26:29.320 --> 00:26:38.420
What did you guys think of, first, that mechanic for stacking on the amount of side-scrolling levels that you, the player, choose to take on?

00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:43.580
Well, I think that, like, theoretically, that adds a little bit of what we were complaining was missing,

00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:50.740
where it's like there's a little bit of thought to go into, like, there's a little bit of purpose for all these different spots on the board,

00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:54.840
where you're like, well, there's the quickest path, but those are the hardest types of level,

00:26:54.840 --> 00:26:59.280
or, like, I'm not good at that type of level, so maybe I can find a path where I don't have to do as many of those.

00:27:00.140 --> 00:27:08.360
Unfortunately, it felt like, so far, I mean, I only got to, like, Jupiter or whatever the third or fourth one was,

00:27:08.440 --> 00:27:12.880
but it's like maybe it gets different later on, but, like, that's, like, halfway through the game, so it's like,

00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:21.520
it felt like, so far, it did not feel like any of those levels were too much more of a problem than any other level.

00:27:21.700 --> 00:27:27.740
I mean, the volcano levels, too, I did try to avoid if I had the opportunity,

00:27:27.740 --> 00:27:36.180
but it didn't let me, it didn't, in practice, didn't make me, like, have to think about a strategy,

00:27:36.180 --> 00:27:43.640
and as far as it going, like, oh, I can only go two, I can only go two, um, two spaces now,

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:46.540
and then I won't have to fight as many levels, which I think is actually the question you asked.

00:27:47.060 --> 00:27:52.980
Um, same thing, though, it felt like, in theory, that's great, it's like, I don't have to go that far,

00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:57.820
because my health's low, but it's not like, after that, you, oh, well, now I get health pickups,

00:27:57.960 --> 00:28:00.060
or something, or now I get something in between levels.

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:01.900
No, I just have to then, next time,

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:05.920
next turn, eventually keep going, and my health is where it was anyways.

00:28:06.180 --> 00:28:08.440
So, it didn't really make a difference.

00:28:08.680 --> 00:28:10.660
Like, it would have, if they, if they had some reason

00:28:10.660 --> 00:28:16.120
to go shorter, and, like, then maybe you get a reward in between to, like, up your health,

00:28:16.140 --> 00:28:19.560
I could see it, but they didn't go all the way with that.

00:28:20.740 --> 00:28:24.680
And, and, yeah, I think, like, yeah, there, it's true that there are different hazards in each

00:28:24.680 --> 00:28:30.260
different, like, biome, um, but, like, the main difference is the coat of paint,

00:28:30.260 --> 00:28:37.260
and, like, while, yeah, there's gonna be a volcano, um, in the volcano ones, there's gonna be another,

00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:45.120
like, vertical, uh, hazard that, that may, that kind of just acts like the volcano, but now it's sort

00:28:45.120 --> 00:28:49.860
of painted like a big vine, um, that's gonna give you just as much trouble.

00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:51.880
Um, so, I, I didn't really

00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:57.000
see too much choice, um, in how, in where you navigated.

00:28:57.140 --> 00:28:58.960
It was just, like, do I want to play

00:28:58.960 --> 00:29:00.660
the green level or the red level?

00:29:01.720 --> 00:29:04.300
Huh. Yeah, I get that.

00:29:04.460 --> 00:29:05.820
Uh, it's also important to mention,

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:11.360
although I, I didn't put, um, much stock into this part of the game, maybe, maybe it would have

00:29:11.360 --> 00:29:15.660
improved my experience, but the side-scrolling levels were just so difficult that I tried not

00:29:15.660 --> 00:29:21.380
to spend a lot of time in them, but apparently, you know, that's how you level up in this game,

00:29:21.500 --> 00:29:28.400
is by doing these side-scrolling levels and, uh, racking up points and then becoming a stronger

00:29:28.400 --> 00:29:31.940
monster, if you will, uh, to take on the other monsters.

00:29:31.940 --> 00:29:34.440
That's only possible in the side-scrolling

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:41.340
levels. I, I'm sure you also theoretically level up because it's point-based, uh, by defeating the

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:47.060
monsters themselves, but it just won't, uh, it won't bring the same amount of points that a side-scrolling

00:29:47.060 --> 00:29:47.940
level could bring.

00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:50.160
That is true.

00:29:50.880 --> 00:29:54.580
Um, I didn't really put all that together at first.

00:29:54.960 --> 00:29:56.200
Um, I didn't

00:29:56.200 --> 00:29:58.900
really, I thought I was just like, oh, I'm on, I'm on level one.

