Um, and then I realized that I was,

00:30:00.980 --> 00:30:03.440
like, still on level one after the first level.

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:07.500
So, um, it, yeah, it, it's definitely, like, you can

00:30:07.500 --> 00:30:16.240
grind, and I think that if you let a, an enemy monster just sort of linger, it will also level

00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:18.200
up, if I'm not mistaken.

00:30:18.980 --> 00:30:25.840
Um, but, uh, I don't know if that added enough depth for me to, to like,

00:30:25.940 --> 00:30:27.600
like, oh, that's why this is there.

00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:31.760
Yeah, because the grind is not particularly fun anyway, so, like,

00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:37.420
you know, like, to, to then level up, like, yeah, you could, you could say, well, you have the choice

00:30:37.420 --> 00:30:42.380
of sticking around and leveling up, or moving on and not being a high level, but sticking around

00:30:42.380 --> 00:30:46.700
leveling up is kind of like the part of the game that I think would get really tedious if you're

00:30:46.700 --> 00:30:47.880
doing it more than you have to.

00:30:48.600 --> 00:30:52.740
So these side-scrolling levels lead up to the monster battles,

00:30:52.740 --> 00:30:59.840
which happen when, uh, your pieces and the, uh, enemy's pieces are next to each other, adjacent to

00:30:59.840 --> 00:31:02.100
each other on any particular hexagon space.

00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:05.600
It asks you if you want to fight this monster, you, I guess

