Did you watch the end?

00:40:01.640 --> 00:40:03.640
No, I was hoping you did.

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:15.760
Okay. Well, the reason why I didn't watch the end is because I heard from a friend that there's a much more compelling and interesting story than the one presented in this game.

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:22.240
Uh, there's actually one that may or may not have really happened to someone in real life.

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:23.880
Sean, do you know what I'm talking about?

00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:30.640
Yeah. So, I, when I was, you know, doing my, like, okay, what are the next couple games?

00:40:31.080 --> 00:40:53.680
Uh, and, you know, just doing some very cursory glances at Wikipedia, uh, I was looking at the Wikipedia entry for Godzilla Monster of Monsters and saw that in popular culture, it described a creepypasta, which for those not in the know is just a spooky story.

00:40:53.680 --> 00:41:01.500
That's, that was originally told online and usually has something to do with pop culture, um, about this game.

00:41:02.140 --> 00:41:06.260
Um, and, uh, there's like, these things are everywhere.

00:41:06.260 --> 00:41:09.740
They're written about everything with varying degrees of quality.

00:41:09.940 --> 00:41:23.660
So, I, I wouldn't usually think anything of it, but, like, this was on the Wikipedia page and has stayed on the Wikipedia page and wasn't, like, removed due to, like, it being, like, not, not very pertinent.

00:41:23.680 --> 00:41:29.800
So, I was like, okay, so this is a pretty, apparently this is one of the most popular of these kinds of stories.

00:41:30.560 --> 00:41:41.600
And it, it details the story of a haunted version of this game that, of course, was found secondhand, um, by a dude.

00:41:41.740 --> 00:41:45.520
Um, I don't know if it's, like, in high school or college or he's an adult.

00:41:45.680 --> 00:41:59.260
I don't know. Um, but, um, it was, he found it in, like, the year 2006 and it looked like a regular, uh, copy of Godzilla Monster of Monsters.

00:41:59.260 --> 00:42:05.440
But, when he started playing it, he noticed that it was, like, you know, glitching out on him, uh, in the bosses.

00:42:06.320 --> 00:42:14.200
And, well, it's, like, you know, it's fading into, like, blood and now, like, the, the HUD is getting all messed up.

00:42:14.300 --> 00:42:16.760
It's like, huh, this is a weird, this is a weird version.

00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:17.680
But, like, no, wait.

00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:19.840
Now there's new monsters.

00:42:21.200 --> 00:42:23.740
Um, some monsters that hadn't even been released yet.

00:42:23.740 --> 00:42:25.720
That's, that's kind of weird, isn't it?

00:42:25.780 --> 00:42:30.100
Like, maybe this is a prototype version, um, or maybe this is a ROM hack.

00:42:30.300 --> 00:42:37.960
And, so, basically, this, this thing keeps escalating to where the game is actually sentient.

00:42:38.640 --> 00:42:42.180
Um, there's a monster in it called Red.

00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:48.320
And there's some, there's some really great, like, amateur writing where it turns out that halfway through,

00:42:48.460 --> 00:42:53.720
he needs to bring up a story that happened earlier in his childhood that was really traumatic about his girlfriend.

00:42:53.740 --> 00:42:57.100
getting hit by, uh, uh, by a car.

00:42:57.360 --> 00:43:01.960
And then it turns out that his girlfriend is being, like, is actually trapped inside the game.

00:43:02.200 --> 00:43:05.880
And then this red guy kills all the monsters.

00:43:05.900 --> 00:43:14.360
And then he, like, when he's playing the game, he actually has, uh, he, he can't physically take the controller out of his hand

00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:17.180
because he's got some mind stuff going on.

00:43:17.300 --> 00:43:20.760
And now the game is asking him questions about if he wants to hurt people.

00:43:20.760 --> 00:43:25.900
And it really is a fascinating read with some really goofy, like, fake screenshots.

00:43:26.300 --> 00:43:33.820
Um, and if you're in the mood for some real amateur hour writing, um, I would look this up.

00:43:34.060 --> 00:43:35.780
It's, it's a lot of fun.

00:43:35.920 --> 00:43:42.400
And it is a little weird at times, but it's, it's too, it's too funny to be actually scary.

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:45.200
Yeah, I don't even know where to go from there.

00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:46.760
Um, that is incredible.

00:43:47.180 --> 00:43:57.820
I, I appreciate people who can, uh, bring this kind of, you know, life to something that otherwise we had nothing really kind to say about,

00:43:57.820 --> 00:44:00.760
uh, you know, Godzilla monster monsters here.

00:44:00.760 --> 00:44:05.580
But now we have an invigorating story about somebody who's been traumatized by the game.

00:44:05.800 --> 00:44:17.820
And actually, um, somebody that was a fan of this story, uh, has apparently at least partially made, um, a video game version of it.

00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:25.000
Um, so, I don't know, look up, uh, yeah, look it up and see if you can fight Red the demon spider.

00:44:25.260 --> 00:44:30.880
I mean, or, or don't if you're a scaredy cat, um, because sometimes these creepypasta things are very strange.

00:44:31.060 --> 00:44:36.420
I'm thinking about that Majora's mask one, uh, that's very creepy with, uh, Ben's copy.

00:44:36.680 --> 00:44:37.900
I think it was or something like that.

00:44:37.960 --> 00:44:39.360
Oh, I've heard of that one. Yeah.

00:44:39.760 --> 00:44:40.580
It's all wild stuff.

00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:43.060
There's Pokemon creepypastas too, right, Joe?

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:44.320
Oh, yeah. Gotta love them.

00:44:44.320 --> 00:44:47.060
Pokemon Black. There's the Lavender Town stuff and...

00:44:49.000 --> 00:45:05.160
Yep. Uh, but I feel like other than that creepypasta, by the way, Sean, the ending of the game is, uh, Godzilla and Mothra are just kind of resting on Planet X as they look back kindly at Planet Earth, realizing that they've rescued it.

00:45:05.300 --> 00:45:09.380
And then you just get a wall of text explaining everything you just did.

00:45:09.880 --> 00:45:15.300
It's just, like, very slowly moving, and it doesn't really add on any additional details.

00:45:15.300 --> 00:45:18.000
Uh, it just says, um...

00:45:18.940 --> 00:45:19.800
Oh, go ahead, Joe.

00:45:19.880 --> 00:45:27.140
Well, I was gonna say, the game really thinks that you, you need to take a lot of time to read this, because it scrolls really slowly at the beginning, too.

00:45:28.200 --> 00:45:29.740
Um... Yeah, I remember that.

00:45:29.740 --> 00:45:33.740
I also just think it's funny that it says that the villains, like, leave, like, a letter.

00:45:34.020 --> 00:45:39.240
They, like, write it like a formal letter that starts out with, to our deepest regret, we must admit defeat.

00:45:39.380 --> 00:45:43.600
Like, and there's, like, stuff later on, too, where it's just, like, very, like, weird.

00:45:43.620 --> 00:45:48.420
It's like they're writing, like, it's like the way they're composing an email professionally to Earth.

00:45:49.560 --> 00:45:51.000
To whom it may concern.

00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:55.920
Yeah, and then it's like, having lost our base, we now embark on a journey to nowhere in the universe.

00:45:56.120 --> 00:45:58.840
But Earthlings, like, it's just, like, so...

00:46:00.200 --> 00:46:02.980
Right, and this isn't even what they said to Godzilla or Mothra.

00:46:03.120 --> 00:46:08.600
This is what they said in the shower later when they were thinking of what they should have said to Godzilla.

00:46:08.600 --> 00:46:17.620
Godzilla. Alright, on the sequels and spinoff side, we do have another Godzilla game.

